   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Kiribati-Australia Education Program in Tungaru (EduKaIT) and in collaboration with the Ministry of Education, the big book project aims to enhance literacy by integrating large-format books into classroom reading lessons. The pilot project has been successfully integrated within day-to-day lessons, supporting 1,601 Year 3 students (almost 2/3rds of students) across three islands including South Tarawa, North Tarawa and Abaiang. 
&#x200d;
The professional development provided to teachers through the project has been demonstrated to be effective, with 100 per cent of schools rated highly for teacher implementation. The books and teaching guides provided to each school have been well received by teachers and students and have contributed to change in teaching strategies and students being more engaged in the learning process. 
&#x200d;
The forthcoming work with the Ministry of Education to develop a literacy strategy will provide clear guidance on further activities, with these early positive changes to teaching practices having positive learning outcomes well into the future.</narrative>
    </description>
